# Issue and feature branches

When you implement an issue or a feature, do the work on a new branch created from an up-to-date `main`. Do not commit that work on `main`.

Name the branch:

```text
cursor/iss-<number>-<brief-description>
```

`<number>` is the GitHub issue number. `<brief-description>` is a short lowercase kebab-case summary of the change. Example: `cursor/iss-248-todays-events`.

When the work has no GitHub issue, omit the issue segment:

```text
cursor/<brief-description>
```

When the work is complete, push the branch and open a pull request into `main`. The pull request description states what changed and why. When the work closes an issue, end the description with `Closes #<number>`. Leave the pull request open for review. Do not merge it.
